    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots naturally into the existing structure of `OwnerMapper`:\n\n- **Right unit, consistent pattern.** `contactPreference` is a derived, read-only field, and the mapper already hosts a family of exactly-analogous `default` derivation methods (`displayName`, `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`) each wired via `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(x(owner))\")`. The new method follows this convention precisely, including the `owner == null` guard and returning `null` in that case.\n- **No duplication.** The email-presence idiom `email != null && !email.isEmpty()` mirrors the identical check already used in `membershipLevel`, so a maintainer would find it familiar; it's a small enough two-line expression that extracting a shared helper would be over-engineering here.\n- **Good placement.** The method is inserted right after `bulkSignupWarning`, keeping the derivation helpers grouped together, and the `@Mapping` line is appended in the same block as its siblings.\n- **Schema addition is coherent.** The `openapi.yml` entry mirrors the other derived read-only fields (`readOnly: true`, description matching the derivation rule), and using a typed `enum`/`ContactPreferenceEnum` rather than a bare string is the idiomatic choice.\n\nNothing is becoming a catch-all and nothing is misplaced.",
